        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>UNIMOD</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>UNIMOD:1001</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Methionine (C5H11NO2S) is substituted in culture with azidohomoalanine (AHA - C4H8N4O2). The azide group reacts with the alkyne group DDDDK-propargylglycine-NH2. As a result the side chain of methionine (C3H7S) is substituted by C29H44N11O14.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>AHA-Alkyne-KDDDD</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
