        <oboInOwl:id>UNIMOD:264</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>PET = 2-[4-pyridyl]ethanethiol. This modification is a chemical derivative, based on a alkaline catalysed beta-elimination of phosphoserines and phosphothreonines and subsequent 1,4-addition of 2-[4-pyridine]ethanethiol. These modified serines and threonines produce in MS/MS a characteristic fragment which can be used for precursor-ion-scan experiments.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>PET</rdfs:label>
