        <oboInOwl:id>UNIMOD:765</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>N-terminal initiator methionine is removed by a methionine aminopeptidase from proteins where the residue following the methionine is Ala, Cys, Gly, Pro, Ser, Thr or Val. This is generally the final N-terminal state for proteins where the following residue was a Cys, Pro or Val.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Met-loss</rdfs:label>
